=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

Per ADR-015, every slice that touches an invariant MUST cite evidence.

  §I1 Default off
    EVIDENCE: NewLimiter and NewCostCap start no goroutines and require
              Quota/CostRepo arguments to be supplied at construction.
              The router-wiring slice (deferred) will only construct
              them in non-off modes. In off mode, guard.Wrap returns
              404 upstream of dispatch.Run, so even a wired chain with
              decorators present is unreachable. Unit tests in
              limiter_test.go / cost_test.go assert that bare
              constructors hold no state until the first Allow / Check.

  §I3 Baseline intact (R8 graceful fallback) — this slice's headline
    EVIDENCE: When a decorator returns *limit.LimitError the dispatcher
              treats it as a NORMAL terminal SSE event (not a Run
              error). The dispatcher's Chat loop catches it via
              errors.As(err, *limit.LimitError) and invokes the
              LimitErrorEmitter (the *stream.Writer satisfies the
              optional interface). The emitted SSE frame carries
              `baseline_available: true` so the page can pivot to its
              non-AI render path immediately. The AiLimitBanner
              renders an explicit "Use baseline" button (gated on
              baselineAvailable) that the page wires to its non-AI
              fallback. Tests:
                - cost_decorator_test.go TestWithCostCap_ReturnsLimitError
                - ratelimit_decorator_test.go TestWithRateLimit_BurstReject
                - AiLimitBanner.test.tsx "shows the baseline button …"

  §I4 Zero outbound egress (HARD)
    EVIDENCE: 1. Decorators perform NO outbound IO. CostCap's only
                 read goes through the CostRepo interface (DB-backed in
                 production via AICallLogTodayAdapter); RateLimit is
                 purely in-memory.
              2. internal/ai/health/ollama_poll.go probes ONLY the
                 user-configured local URL via the injected Doer
                 interface; no third-party calls. The prompt's local
                 mode policy already vetted this surface in F1.
              3. AiLimitBanner is presentational; no fetch / no
                 imperative network. The countdown uses setInterval
                 against a local seconds counter only.

  §I5 No raw SQL mutation outside repo
    EVIDENCE: F9 introduces NO new SQL. CostCap consumes the existing
              *AICallLogRepo.Today read path (parameterised, $1..$N).
              No new migrations, no string-interpolated SQL.

  §I6 404 in off mode
    EVIDENCE: F9 adds NO new HTTP routes. The new decorators wrap
              existing provider methods that are already gated upstream
              by guard.Wrap. The Ollama poller is internal — no HTTP
              surface exposed to clients.

  §I7 Per-feature opt-in (fail loud on misconfig)
    EVIDENCE: limit.Limiter.Allow rejects unknown OR missing FeatureID
              with typed reasons unknown_feature_id /
              missing_feature_id (both surface in the SSE error frame
              and in AiLimitBanner copy). A page that forgot to wire
              its feature ID will see an immediate banner — never
              silent over-quota use. Tests:
                - limiter_test.go TestLimiter_RejectsMissingFeatureID
                - limiter_test.go TestLimiter_RejectsUnknownFeatureID
                - AiLimitBanner.test.tsx "renders the right title for
                  reason=missing_feature_id" and "…unknown_feature_id"

  §I8 Downgrade survives (mode flip clears nothing dangerous)
    EVIDENCE: Limiter buckets live in-memory only and are scoped per
              (subject, featureID); a mode flip from cloud→off does
              not need to touch them — the next call is gated upstream
              by guard.Wrap. The cost cap setting (ai_cost_cap_cents)
              is persisted via the existing AISettings save path; F9
              only reads it. Flipping mode and back preserves the cap
              value and the spend bar resumes correctly.

  §I9 Provenance visible
    EVIDENCE: The reason taxonomy is rendered as a stable, searchable
              phrase in AiLimitBanner (cost_cap, per_minute, burst,
              etc.). The AISettings cost-cap spend bar surfaces the
              user's daily $ position with a colour-coded threshold
              (>=80% amber, >=100% rose) so the user can see exhaustion
              coming. The bar's data-spend-level attribute exposes the
              level for downstream selectors / e2e tests.

  §I10 No silent network egress (UI side)
    EVIDENCE: AiLimitBanner has no fetch / no imperative network. Its
              countdown uses a local setInterval. The spend bar in
              AISettings uses the EXISTING useAiUsageToday() hook —
              same surface AIUsageCard already calls. No new endpoints
              hit; no new envelope shapes invented.

  §I12 Auditable (background re-checks mode)
    EVIDENCE: OllamaPoller is designed to be constructed only when the
              local provider is in use. The poller's tick() respects
              the injected Suspender contract — when ai_mode flips to
              off, the future router-wiring slice will stop the poller
              (Cancel context). The poller never persists state and
              never calls Tesla / cloud providers; its only side effect
              is calling SuspendProvider on the limiter.

  §I7 + Forward dependency (decorators-as-building-blocks)
    EVIDENCE: F9 ships the decorators (WithRateLimit, WithCostCap) and
              the dispatcher's errors.As detection PATH but does NOT
              wire the decorators into the registry chain. router.go +
              registry.go are NOT in this slice's allowed-files list,
              so wiring is deferred to the first consuming feature
              slice (e.g. U1) that needs the limits. The dispatcher's
              integration is dormant-but-correct: once registered, the
              Chat loop's errors.As branch will trigger and emit
              structured SSE limit frames without further dispatcher
              changes. This mirrors the F1 precedent where Audit /
              Trace decorators shipped before being added to the
              registry chain. Documented under === REASONING === point
              10 above.


